sentences.l:
But having washed, and taken clean garments for your skin,
having gone up to the upper chamber with your attendant women,
pray to Athena, daughter of aegis-bearing Zeus;

And she, having washed, and taken clean garments for her skin,
went up to the upper chamber with her attendant women,
and put barley-grains in a basket, and prayed to Athena;

And as many things as a lion ponders, in a throng of men,
being afraid, whenever they lead around him a treacherous circle,
so many things, as she pondered, sweet sleep came upon her;

The gods, who live at ease, do not allow you
to weep nor to be grieved, since still there is a homecoming for
your son;

who first lost a noble husband, lion-hearted,
distinguished by virtues of every kind among the Danaans,
noble — whose fame is wide throughout Hellas and mid-Argos;

for such a guide goes with him, whom also other
men have prayed to stand beside them, for she is able,
Pallas Athena;

And there is a certain island, rocky, in the middle of the sea,
between Ithaca and rugged Same,
Asteris, not large;
